        "value": "Binary politeness distinction",
        "source": "wals-v2020.5",
        "note": "<div class=\"Example\"><table class=\"example\"><tr><td><p><i>na</i></p></td><td><p>2nd sg. hon.</p></td><td><p>- these plural pronouns are not used for normal</p><p>conversational politeness (e.g. with a stranger of more-</p><p>or-less equal status) in the way that French <i>vous</i> or</p><p>German <i>Sie</i> are; here the singular forms are always</p><p>found;</p><p>- it seems that the chief of the village is the</p><p>lowest social rank for which the plurals are used.</p></td></tr></table></div>",
        "scale": "wals-v2020.5"
